### requests.http — every endpoint, ready to send.
###
### VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then click "Send Request"
### above any request. PhpStorm and other JetBrains IDEs run this file natively.
### Each request is separated by ###. Change @base if you serve the API elsewhere,
### e.g. http://localhost/backend-kit on XAMPP.

@base = http://localhost:8000

### The API map
GET {{base}}/

### List every bookmark
GET {{base}}/api/bookmarks

### One bookmark
GET {{base}}/api/bookmarks/1

### Create one: expect 201 Created and a Location header
POST {{base}}/api/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "HTTP status codes",
  "url": "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Status",
  "note": "Every code this API returns is in here"
}

### Change only the note: expect 200 and the updated bookmark
PATCH {{base}}/api/bookmarks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "note": "Changed with PATCH"
}

### Delete one: expect 204 No Content, then 404 if you send it again
DELETE {{base}}/api/bookmarks/2

### ---- Requests that should fail, and why ----

### 422: fields fail validation (and javascript: is refused)
POST {{base}}/api/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "url": "javascript:alert(1)",
  "note": 42
}

### 400: not valid JSON (trailing comma)
POST {{base}}/api/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Broken", }

### 415: right data, wrong Content-Type (this is how an HTML form sends)
POST {{base}}/api/bookmarks
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

title=Form&url=https://example.com

### 404: no such bookmark
GET {{base}}/api/bookmarks/99999

### 405: the address exists, the method doesn't. Read the Allow header.
PUT {{base}}/api/bookmarks/1
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### CORS preflight, as a browser at http://localhost:5500 would send it
OPTIONS {{base}}/api/bookmarks
Origin: http://localhost:5500
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
Access-Control-Request-Headers: content-type
